          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Grothendieck fibration
            (named after
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"} Alexander Grothendieck
            %em fibered category
            or just a
            = succeed ")" do
              %em fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon E\to B
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_b = p^{-1}(b)
            depend (contravariantly)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctorially
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
          %p
            One also says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a
            %em fibered category
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            the
            %em total category
            of the fibration (not to be confused with the independent notion of
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+category"} total category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            its
            = succeed "." do
              %em base category
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"}> Dually
            , in a (Grothendieck)
            %em opfibration
            the dependence is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+functor"} covariant
          %p
            There is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} 2-categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Fib
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↔
                    %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mo ∫
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Fib(B)
                  \\overset
                  {\simeq}
                  {\leftrightarrow}
                  [B^{op}, Cat]
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\textstyle{\int}
          %p
            between the 2-category of fibrations, cartesian functors, and vertical natural transformations over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
